                    ← parent = Cloud id\n │   └─ [Virtual Network] (VPC|VNet)   ← parent = Region id\n │       ├─ [Load Balancer / Gateway]  ← parent = VPC id (sibling of Zones)\n │       ├─ [Zone] × N                 ← parent = VPC id\n │       │   ├─ [Public Subnet]        ← parent = Zone id\n │       │   ├─ [Private App Subnet]   ← parent = Zone id\n │       │   └─ [Private Data Subnet]  ← parent = Zone id\n │       │       └─ [service icons]    ← parent = Subnet id\n │       ├─ [Security Group]           ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       ├─ [Monitoring Group]         ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       ├─ [Integration Group]        ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       └─ [Management Group]         ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n └─ [Edge/Global Layer]                ← parent = Cloud id (sibling of Region, still INSIDE Cloud)\n     └─ DNS / CDN / WAF / static       ← parent = Edge layer id\n```\n\n**Outer-layer wrap rules:**\n1. Create the Cloud boundary first. Its `parent="1"`. Size it large enough to contain Region + Edge + padding.\n2. Region is **inside** Cloud (`parent=<cloud-id>`). VPC is **inside** Region. Zones/subnets/groups are **inside** VPC. Services are **inside** their subnet or supporting group.\n3. **FORBIDDEN:** Region, VPC, Zone, Subnet, Security/Monitoring/Integration/Management, or Edge as `parent="1"` siblings floating beside the Cloud box. If it belongs in the hierarchy, it must be a child of the layer above it.\n4. **FORBIDDEN:** placing an inner box with absolute canvas coordinates while `parent="1"` so it only overlaps the outer box visually. Overlap ≠ containment.\n5. Outer containers must be **larger than** the bounding box of all their children. Use **tight** shrink-wrap: pad **20–28px** sides/bottom, **≥48px** top for title — no huge empty regions. Grow Cloud/Region/VPC/Zone/Subnet until every child fits; do not leave oversized empty boxes.\n6. Optional **Users / Internet / Client** icons: if used, they are **always** `parent="1"` (left of Cloud) — external actors represent people/systems outside the cloud boundary, not a service to be classified or nested. Everything else cloud-related stays wrapped inside Cloud.\n7. **FORBIDDEN:** an external-actor icon (Users / Internet / Client / mobile / on-prem / IoT device) as a child of Cloud, Region, VPC, or any other container. It never has a classification decision — it is not a service.\n\n## Leaf Footprint — UNDER-ICON LABELS (CRITICAL)\n\nService leaves use `verticalLabelPosition=bottom` — the **label draws below** the icon box. Parent sizing must account for that extra band, not only the 78×78 icon geometry.\n\n- Icon size: 78×78 main, 65×65 secondary\n- Under-label band: leave **≥ 32–40px** clear space below the icon inside the parent (labels must not kiss the subnet border or the next row)\n- Labels may be **wider than the icon** (assume up to ~120px centered) → ~21px overhang each side. Adjacent icons must use enough pitch so overhangs do not collide\n- Parent width must include: last icon `x + max(icon.width, ~labelWidth) + pad` — not merely `x + 78`\n- Parent height must include: `child.y + child.height + labelBand + pad`\n- Self-check: every child\'s **icon and under-label** fit insi... (truncated, 27382 total chars)', 'human_content': 'Platform: AWS\nRequest:\nHighly available web app with load balancer, app servers in private subnets across multiple AZs, managed database with read replicas, CDN for static assets, cache layer, WAF, DNS routing, and CloudWatch monitoring'}
